 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 598 of the laws of 1938 relating to incorporating the\nvolunteer and exempt firemen's benevolent association of Briarcliff Manor, New\nYork, and providing for its powers and duties, in relation to changing the\nform of the benevolent from a corporation to an unincorporated association",
    "basePrintNo": "S8531",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8531-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1-8, Chap 598 of 1938",
    "lawSection": "Westchester County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8531\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 598 of the laws of 1938 relating to incorporat-\ning the volunteer and exempt firemen's benevolent association of Briar-\ncliff Manor, New York, and providing for its powers and duties, in\nrelation to changing the form of the benevolent from a corporation to an\nunincorporated association\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to change the Volunteer and Exempt\nFiremens Benevolent Association of Briarcliff Manor, New York\n\n(VEFBABMNY) from a corporation to an unincorpdrated association.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends sections 1-8 of chapter 598 of the laws of 1938 by\nchanging firemens's to firefighters'. It also names the purpose of the\nassociation in greater detail, transfers certain noticing duties from\nthe village clerk of Briarcliff Manor to the secretary of the associ-\nation, and replaces corporation with association in numerous places.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nThis section is not applicable at this time.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe VEFBABMNY is requesting special legislation to change their status\nfrom a corporation to an unincorporation since it has been operating as\none from its inception in 1938.\n\nOriginally, the VEFBABMNY was created as a membership corporation.\nHowever, the corporation was never created, and instead the VEFBABMNY\nhas been operating as an unincorporated association.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThere are no fiscal implications associated with the passage of this\nlegislation.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
